        "original_id": "ef3f4a19-5a52-50e7-aa97-c177af68d5b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals and Waterways: Hampshire and Hampden Canal, Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway, Farmington Canal\n- Places: Massachusetts, Connecticut, New Haven, Northampton, Alabama, Demopolis, Boston\n- People: Tim Barsky\n\nFacts:\n- The Hampshire and Hampden Canal was the Massachusetts segment of an 86-mile canal that once connected New Haven, Connecticut, to the Connecticut River north of Northampton, Massachusetts.\n- The Farmington Canal's Massachusetts segment was known as the Hampshire and Hampden Canal.\n- The Tennessee–Tombigbee Waterway, also called the Tenn-Tom, is a 234-mile man-made waterway that extends from the Tennessee River to the junction of the Black Warrior-Tombigbee River system near Demopolis, Alabama.\n- Tim Barsky is an American musician from Boston, Massachusetts.",
